        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "07cc7bef-b849-552b-aa93-48092a78bd94",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Torra di Tizzà, North Africa, Salé, Rabat, Algiers, Tunis, Tripoli\n- Organizations: Republic of Genoa\n- Groups: Barbary pirates, Barbary corsairs, Ottoman corsairs\n- Systems: coastal defences\n- Topics: piracy, privateering\n\nFacts:\n- The Republic of Genoa constructed a series of coastal defences between 1530 and 1620 to stem attacks by Barbary pirates.\n- Torra di Tizzà was one of the coastal defences that the Republic of Genoa constructed between 1530 and 1620.\n- The Barbary pirates were also called Barbary corsairs and Ottoman corsairs.\n- The Barbary pirates were pirates and privateers who operated from North Africa.\n- The Barbary pirates were based primarily in the ports of Salé, Rabat, Algiers, Tunis, and Tripoli.",
